# The content list — docs/proposals/world.md §13.1: a selected module list and
# normal Gene loading.
#
# **One list, and this is it.** The world process calls `load_mods` once and
# reads the registries off the `Content` it gets back. The browser client does
# not: it is handed the registries over the wire (server-selected content,
# §15.6).
#
# Content here is trusted code in this package, compiled in like any other
# module. There is no runtime loader and no grant model (§1.2, §1.4).
#
# `^profile web` keeps the module portable, so a web-profile spec can register
# the same content the server does.

(mod mods ^profile web)

(import [Content new_content] ^from "./content.gene")
(import [register_all] ^from "../mods/neighborhood/src/neighborhood.gene")

# The content, registered. Called once per process, before anything reads a
# content id: ids are assigned as modules register, in this list's order, and
# a module added later must come after the ones already here. A saved region
# keeps node names, not ids (§5.3), so it means the same thing either way.
(fn load_mods [] : Content
  (var content (new_content))
  (register_all content)
  content)
